ontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-25T11:48:56Z","updated_at":"2025-07-25T11:48:56Z","body":"> LGTM, only small question is if it's safe to hardcode `true` in a few calls to `_rt_attach_textures`, instead of checking `render_target_get_depth_has_stencil`.\r\n\r\nBastiaan and I chatted about this on RocketChat, so a note for folks only following GitHub:\r\n\r\nThe hard-coded `true` is in the case where we've allocated an intermediate depth buffer for MSAA (and we always allocate those with a format that has a stencil component); we only need to check `render_target_get_depth_has_stencil()` for the case where we are rendering directly to the render target, which may have a depth buffer allocated by WebXR","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3117495917/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]